"  CCARGS=\"$CCARGS -DHAS_CDB\"\n"
"  AUXLIBS=\"$AUXLIBS <replaceable>&lt;/path/to/CDB&gt;</replaceable>/libcdb.a\"\n"
"fi</literal>"
msgstr ""
"<literal>if [ -r <replaceable>&lt;/path/to/CDB&gt;</replaceable>/libcdb.a ]; then\n"
"  CCARGS=\"$CCARGS -DHAS_CDB\"\n"
"  AUXLIBS=\"$AUXLIBS <replaceable>&lt;/path/to/CDB&gt;</replaceable>/libcdb.a\"\n"
"fi</literal>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><title>
#: blfs-en/server/mail/postfix.xml:298
#, xml-text
msgid "StartTLS Authentication"
msgstr "Autenticação StartTLS"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><para>
#: blfs-en/server/mail/postfix.xml:301
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"To use <application>OpenSSL</application> with "
"<application>Postfix</application>, use the following arguments:"
msgstr ""
"Para usar o &quot;<application>OpenSSL</application>&quot; com o "
"&quot;<application>Postfix</application>&quot;, use os seguintes argumentos:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><screen>
#: blfs-en/server/mail/postfix.xml:305
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>if [ -r /usr/lib/libssl.so -a -r /usr/lib/libcrypto.so ]; then\n"
"  CCARGS=\"$CCARGS -DUSE_TLS -I/usr/include/openssl/\"\n"
"  AUXLIBS=\"$AUXLIBS -lssl -lcrypto\"\n"
"fi</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>if [ -r /usr/lib/libssl.so -a -r /usr/lib/libcrypto.so ]; then\n"
"  CCARGS=\"$CCARGS -DUSE_TLS -I/usr/include/openssl/\"\n"
"  AUXLIBS=\"$AUXLIBS -lssl -lcrypto\"\n"
"fi</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><sect4><para>
#: blfs-en/server/mail/postfix.xml:310
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<application>OpenSSL</application> is installed by LFS so it should be "
"always there. The <code>if ... then</code> is here just for consistency."
msgstr ""
"<application>OpenSSL</application> é instalado pelo LFS, de forma que ele "
"deveria estar sempre lá. O <code>if ... then</code> está aqui apenas para "
"consistência."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><title>
#: blfs-en/server/mail/postfix.xml:319
#, xml-text
msgid "Installing Postfix"
msgstr "Instalando o Postfix"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/server/mail/postfix.xml:322
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"There might be duplicate settings in <envar>AUXLIBS</envar> like "
"<code>-lm</code> when both, <application>MariaDB</application> and "
"<application>PostgreSQL</application> are used. They do not harm. Install "
"<application>Postfix</application> by running the following commands:"
msgstr ""
"Podem existir configurações duplicadas em <envar>AUXLIBS</envar>, como "
"<code>-lm</code>, quando ambos, <application>MariaDB</application> e "
"<application>PostgreSQL</application> são usados. Elas não danificam. "
"Instale o <application>Postfix</application> executando os seguintes "
"comandos:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/server/mail/postfix.xml:329
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>make CCARGS=\"$CCARGS\" AUXLIBS=\"$AUXLIBS\" makefiles &amp;&amp;\n"
"make</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>make CCARGS=\"$CCARGS\" AUXLIBS=\"$AUXLIBS\" makefiles &amp;&amp;\n"
"make</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/server/mail/postfix.xml:336
#, xml-text
msgid "This package does not come with a useful test suite."
msgstr "Esse pacote não vem com uma suíte de teste útil."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/server/mail/postfix.xml:340
#, xml-text
msgid "Now, as the <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""
"Agora, como o(a) usuário(a) &quot;<systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem>&quot;:"

#.  dev note: sh postfix-install -non-interactive install_root=<DESTDIR>
#.  ...
#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/server/mail/postfix.xml:345
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>sh postfix-install -non-interactive \\\n"
"   daemon_directory=/usr/lib/postfix \\\n"
"   manpage_directory=/usr/share/man \\\n"
"   html_directory=/usr/share/doc/postfix-&postfix-version;/html \\\n"
"   readme_directory=/usr/share/doc/postfix-&postfix-version;/readme</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>sh postfix-install -non-interactive \\\n"
"  daemon_directory=/usr/lib/postfix \\\n"
"  manpage_directory=/usr/share/man \\\n"
"  html_directory=/usr/share/doc/postfix-&postfix-version;/html \\\n"
"  readme_directory=/usr/share/doc/postfix-&postfix-version;/readme</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/server/mail/postfix.xml:356
#, xml-text
msgid "Command Explanations"
msgstr "Explicações do Comando"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/server/mail/postfix.xml:359
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<command>make makefiles</command>: This command rebuilds the makefiles "
"throughout the source tree to use the options contained in the "
"<envar>CCARGS</envar> and <envar>AUXLIBS</envar> variables."
msgstr ""
"<command>make makefiles</command>: Esse comando reconstrói os "
"&quot;makefiles&quot; em toda a árvore fonte para usar as opções contidas "
"nas variáveis &quot;<envar>CCARGS</envar>&quot; e "
"&quot;<envar>AUXLIBS</envar>&quot;."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/server/mail/postfix.xml:365
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<command>sh postfix-install -non-interactive</command>: This keeps the "
"install script from asking any questions, thereby accepting default "
"destination directories in all but the few cases. If the "
"<option>html_directory</option> and <option>readme_directory</option> "
"options are not set then the documentation will not be installed."
msgstr ""
"<command>sh postfix-install -non-interactive</command>: Isso evita que o "
"conjunto de comandos sequenciais de instalação faça perguntas, aceitando "
"assim os diretórios de destino padrão em todos os casos, exceto em uns "
"poucos. Se as opções &quot;<option>html_directory</option>&quot; e "
"&quot;<option>readme_directory</option>&quot; não estiverem configuradas, "
"[então] a documentação não será instalada."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/server/mail/postfix.xml:373
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<option>CCARGS=\"-DNO_EAI ...\"</option>: this will turn off SMTPUTF8 "
"support, for example if the rest of your email address infrastructure cannot"
" handle UTF-8 email addresses and message header values."
msgstr ""
"<option>CCARGS=\"-DNO_EAI ...\"</option>: isso desligará o suporte a "
"SMTPUTF8, por exemplo, se o restante da tua infraestrutura de endereço de "
"correio eletrônico não puder lidar com endereços UTF-8 de correio eletrônico"
" e valores de cabeçalho de mensagem."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/server/mail/postfix.xml:381
#, xml-text
msgid "Configuring Postfix"
msgstr "Configurando o Postfix"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><title>
#: blfs-en/server/mail/postfix.xml:384
#, xml-text
msgid "Config Files"
msgstr "Arquivos de Configuração"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/server/mail/postfix.xml:387
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<filename>/etc/aliases</filename>, "
"<filename>/etc/postfix/main.cf</filename>, and "
"<filename>/etc/postfix/master.cf</filename>"
msgstr ""
"<filename>/etc/aliases</filename>, <filename>/etc/postfix/main.cf</filename>"
" e <filename>/etc/postfix/master.cf</filename>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><indexterm><primary>
#: blfs-en/server/mail/postfix.xml:393
#, xml-text
msgid "/etc/aliases"
msgstr "/etc/aliases"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><indexterm><primary>
#: blfs-en/server/mail/postfix.xml:397
#, xml-text
msgid "/etc/postfix/*"
msgstr "/etc/postfix/*"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><title>
#: blfs-en/server/mail/postfix.xml:403
#, xml-text
msgid "Configuration Information"
msgstr "Informação de Configuração"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/server/mail/postfix.xml:406
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Create (or append to an existing) <filename>/etc/aliases</filename> with the"
" following command. Change <replaceable>&lt;LOGIN&gt;</replaceable> to your "
"non-root login identity so mail addressed to <systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem> can be forwarded to you.  As the "
"<systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""
"Crie (ou anexe a um existente) &quot;<filename>/etc/aliases</filename>&quot;"
" com o seguinte comando. Mude "
"&quot;<replaceable>&lt;LOGIN&gt;</replaceable>&quot; para a tua identidade "
"de login não &quot;root&quot; de forma que as mensagens endereçadas para "
"o(a) &quot;<systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem>&quot; possam ser"
" encaminhadas para você. Como o(a) usuário(a) &quot;<systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem>&quot;:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/server/mail/postfix.xml:414
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>cat &gt;&gt; /etc/aliases &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Begin /etc/aliases\n"
"\n"
"MAILER-DAEMON:    postmaster\n"
"postmaster:       root\n"
"\n"
"root:             <replaceable>&lt;LOGIN&gt;</replaceable>\n"
"# End /etc/aliases</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>cat &gt;&gt; /etc/aliases &lt;&lt; \"EOF\"\n"
"<literal># Inicia /etc/aliases\n"
"\n"
"MAILER-DAEMON:    postmaster\n"
"postmaster:       root\n"
"\n"
"root:             <replaceable>&lt;LOGIN&gt;</replaceable>\n"
"# Termina /etc/aliases</literal>\n"
"EOF</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/server/mail/postfix.xml:425
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"To protect an existing <filename>/etc/aliases</filename> file, the above "
"command appends these aliases to it if it exists. This file should be "
"checked and duplicate aliases removed, if present."
msgstr ""
"Para proteger um arquivo &quot;<filename>/etc/aliases</filename>&quot; "
"existente, o comando acima anexa esses apelidos a ele, se existir. Esse "
"arquivo deveria ser verificado e os apelidos duplicados removidos, se "
"presentes."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/server/mail/postfix.xml:431
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"The BLFS editors recommend to use LMDB instead of Berkeley DB for Postfix "
"tables.  Add three lines into <filename>/etc/postfix/main.cf</filename> to "
"make <command>postmap</command> encode the lookup tables in the LMDB format "
"by default and to change the default hash setting of the alias tables:"
msgstr ""
"Os(As) editores(as) do BLFS recomendam usar LMDB em vez de Berkeley DB para "
"tabelas do Postfix. Adicione três linhas em "
"<filename>/etc/postfix/main.cf</filename> para fazer com que "
"<command>postmap</command> codifique as tabelas de pesquisa no formato do "
"LMDB por padrão e para mudar a configuração padrão de resumo das tabelas de "
"apelidos:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/server/mail/postfix.xml:439
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>echo 'default_database_type = lmdb'       &gt;&gt; /etc/postfix/main.cf &amp;&amp;\n"
"echo 'alias_database = lmdb:/etc/aliases' &gt;&gt; /etc/postfix/main.cf &amp;&amp;\n"
"echo 'alias_maps = lmdb:/etc/aliases'     &gt;&gt; /etc/postfix/main.cf</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>echo 'default_database_type = lmdb'       &gt;&gt; /etc/postfix/main.cf &amp;&amp;\n"
"echo 'alias_database = lmdb:/etc/aliases' &gt;&gt; /etc/postfix/main.cf &amp;&amp;\n"
"echo 'alias_maps = lmdb:/etc/aliases'     &gt;&gt; /etc/postfix/main.cf</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/server/mail/postfix.xml:444
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"To protect your server against the recent SMTP smuggling attacks, additional"
" steps are required. Add two lines into "
"<filename>/etc/postfix/main.cf</filename> to disconnect remote SMTP clients "
"that send bare newlines in the DATA section, while also allowing clients on "
"your network with non-standard SMTP implementations to still send mail:"
msgstr ""
"Para proteger teu servidor contra os recentes ataques de contrabando de "
"SMTP, etapas adicionais são exigidas. Adicione duas linhas em "
"<filename>/etc/postfix/main.cf</filename> para desconectar clientes SMTP "
"remotos que enviem novas linhas simples na seção DATA, ao mesmo tempo que "
"permite que clientes em tua rede de intercomunicação com implementações SMTP"
" não padrão ainda enviem mensagens:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/server/mail/postfix.xml:452
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>echo 'smtpd_forbid_bare_newline = normalize' &gt;&gt; /etc/postfix/main.cf &amp;&amp;\n"
"echo 'smtpd_forbid_bare_newline_exclusions = $mynetworks' &gt;&gt; /etc/postfix/main.cf</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>echo 'smtpd_forbid_bare_newline = normalize' &gt;&gt; /etc/postfix/main.cf &amp;&amp;\n"
"echo 'smtpd_forbid_bare_newline_exclusions = $mynetworks' &gt;&gt; /etc/postfix/main.cf</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/server/mail/postfix.xml:456
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Note that if you are following an online tutorial to configure Postfix, the "
"tutorial may refer to a lookup table with "
"<literal>hash:/path/to/lookup_table</literal>.  You should replace "
"<literal>hash</literal> with <literal>lmdb</literal> in order to use a "
"lookup table encoded in the LMDB format."
msgstr ""
"Observe que se você estiver seguindo um tutorial online para configurar o "
"Postfix, o tutorial pode se referir a uma tabela de pesquisa com "
"<literal>hash:/caminho/para/tabela_pesquisa</literal>. Você deveria "
"substituir <literal>hash</literal> por <literal>lmdb</literal> para a "
"finalidade de usar uma tabela de pesquisa codificada no formato do LMDB."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><note><para>
#: blfs-en/server/mail/postfix.xml:465
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"The <filename>/etc/postfix/main.cf</filename> and "
"<filename>/etc/postfix/master.cf</filename> files must be personalized for "
"your system. The <filename>main.cf</filename> file needs your fully "
"qualified hostname. You will find that <filename>main.cf</filename> is self "
"documenting, so load it into your editor to make the changes you need for "
"your situation."
msgstr ""
"Os arquivos &quot;<filename>/etc/postfix/main.cf</filename>&quot; e "
"&quot;<filename>/etc/postfix/master.cf</filename>&quot; precisam ser "
"personalizados para o teu sistema. O arquivo "
"&quot;<filename>main.cf</filename>&quot; precisa do teu nome de dispositivo "
"totalmente qualificado. Você descobrirá que "
"&quot;<filename>main.cf</filename>&quot; é auto documentado, de forma que "
"carregue-o em teu editor para fazer as mudanças necessárias para a tua "
"situação."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><note><para>
#: blfs-en/server/mail/postfix.xml:476
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<application>Postfix</application> can also be set up to run in a chroot "
"jail. See the file in the source <filename>examples/chroot-"
"setup/LINUX2</filename> for details."
msgstr ""
"O &quot;<application>Postfix</application>&quot; também pode ser configurado"
" para executar em uma jaula &quot;chroot&quot;. Veja-se o arquivo no fonte "
"&quot;<filename>examples/chroot-setup/LINUX2</filename>&quot; para detalhes."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/server/mail/postfix.xml:483
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"To ensure that all permissions are set properly, "
"<application>postfix</application> provides a tool which is to be run as the"
" <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""
"Para garantir que todas as permissões sejam configuradas corretamente, o "
"<application>postfix</application> fornece uma ferramenta que é para ser "
"executada como o(a) usuário(a) <systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem>:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/server/mail/postfix.xml:488
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>/usr/sbin/postfix -c /etc/postfix set-permissions</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>/usr/sbin/postfix -c /etc/postfix set-permissions</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/server/mail/postfix.xml:491
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If you have an existing configuration, you can run the "
"<command>postfix</command> utility to add any necessary definitions to your "
"existing files. As the <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> "
"user:"
msgstr ""
"Se você tiver uma configuração existente, [então] poderá executar o "
"utilitário &quot;<command>postfix</command>&quot; para adicionar quaisquer "
"definições necessárias aos teus arquivos existentes. Como o(a) usuário(a) "
"&quot;<systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem>&quot;:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/server/mail/postfix.xml:497
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>/usr/sbin/postfix upgrade-configuration</userinput>"
msgstr "<userinput>/usr/sbin/postfix upgrade-configuration</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/server/mail/postfix.xml:500
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Before starting <application>Postfix</application>, you should check that "
"your configuration and file permissions will work properly. Run the "
"following commands as the <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> "
"user to check and start your <application>Postfix</application> server:"
msgstr ""
"Antes de iniciar o &quot;<application>Postfix</application>&quot;, você "
"deveria verificar se a tua configuração e permissões de arquivo funcionarão "
"adequadamente. Execute os seguintes comandos como o(a) usuário(a) "
"&quot;<systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem>&quot; para verificar "
"e iniciar o teu servidor &quot;<application>Postfix</application>&quot;:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/server/mail/postfix.xml:506
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>/usr/sbin/postfix check &amp;&amp;\n"
"/usr/sbin/postfix start</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>/usr/sbin/postfix check &amp;&amp;\n"
"/usr/sbin/postfix start</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><title>
#: blfs-en/server/mail/postfix.xml:512
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<phrase revision=\"sysv\">Boot Script</phrase> <phrase "
"revision=\"systemd\">Systemd Unit</phrase>"
msgstr ""
"<phrase revision=\"sysv\">Conjunto de Comandos Sequenciais de "
"Inicialização</phrase> <phrase revision=\"systemd\">Unidade do "
"systemd</phrase>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><para>
#: blfs-en/server/mail/postfix.xml:516
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"To automate the running of Postfix at startup, install the <phrase "
"revision=\"sysv\"><filename>/etc/rc.d/init.d/postfix</filename> init "
"script</phrase> <phrase "
"revision=\"systemd\"><filename>postfix.service</filename> unit</phrase> "
"included in the <xref linkend=\"bootscripts\" revision=\"sysv\"/> <xref "
"linkend=\"systemd-units\" revision=\"systemd\"/> package:"
msgstr ""
"Para automatizar a execução do &quot;Postfix&quot; na inicialização, instale"
" <phrase revision=\"sysv\">o conjunto de comandos sequenciais de "
"inicialização &quot;<filename>/etc/rc.d/init.d/postfix</filename>&quot; "
"incluso</phrase> <phrase revision=\"systemd\">a unidade "
"&quot;<filename>postfix.service</filename>&quot; inclusa</phrase> no pacote "
"&quot;<xref linkend=\"bootscripts\" revision=\"sysv\"/>&quot; &quot;<xref "
"linkend=\"systemd-units\" revision=\"systemd\"/>&quot;:"

#. type: Content of:
#. <sect1><sect2><variablelist><varlistentry><listitem><indexterm><primary>
#: blfs-en/server/mail/postfix.xml:526 blfs-en/server/mail/postfix.xml:648
#, xml-text
msgid "postfix"
msgstr "postfix"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><sect3><screen>
#: blfs-en/server/mail/postfix.xml:529
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>make install-postfix</userinput>"
msgstr "<userinput>make install-postfix</userinput>"

